                <pb facs="0166" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867n.404Wailing Wall/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-25T15:00:00-04:00">August 25, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your August 24, 7 p.m., was received last night at 10:52 o’clock. It should be
                    emphasized by you with the competent British authorities that they are
                    responsible for protecting American lives and property in Palestine.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
